      "card_ids": ["C157"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L5 shows related quinones/naphthoquinones have high permeability and no significant net efflux (NSC745885 Papp A-B 31.8e-6 cm/s; plumbagin 10.29-15.96e-6 cm/s), supporting absorption capacity.",
      "card_ids": ["C171", "C174"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L6 adds hepatic metabolic-stability context: related naphthoquinones (buparvaquone/58C80, 2-hydroxy-3-phenyl-1,4-naphthoquinone, iodo analog) undergo CYP2C9/2C8-mediated metabolism with moderate intrinsic clearance, a mechanistic concern for presystemic loss, but no direct query hepatic clearance is reported.",
      "card_ids": ["C241", "C254", "C215", "C230", "C257"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "No affirmative threshold-relevant evidence supports F<20% for the query; the metabolic-liability concern is indirect and transfer-limited, so the prediction remains high.",
      "card_ids": ["C241", "C254", "C215", "C230", "C257"]
    }
  ],
  "new_evidence_assessment": [
    {
      "family": "hepatic_clearance_metabolic_stability",
      "applicability": "low",
      "direction": "contradictory",
      "decision_effect": "weakened",
      "card_ids": ["C241", "C254", "C215", "C230", "C257"]
    }
  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct oral bioavailability measurement for the query molecule.",
    "No matched oral versus intravenous exposure data for the query.",
    "No fed-state-specific absorption, solubility, or dissolution data for the query.",
    "No direct hepatic clearance or metabolic-stability data for atovaquone itself; L6 records are for structurally related naphthoquinones.",
    "No direct gut-wall efflux or intestinal-metabolism data for atovaquone.",
    "Structural similarity between the query and all L1 reference molecules is limited."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "Predicted high because all direct L1 gold outcomes are >=20%, L4/L5 indicate a permeability-capable but solubility-limited naphthoquinone class with no efflux barrier, and L6 metabolic-liability evidence for analogs is indirect and does not affirmatively establish F<20%; the fed-state condition is expected to improve absorption. Confidence remains low due to lack of query-specific measurements."
}

